<!--
TEMPLATE: templates/pages/source-summary.md.template
RENDERS TO: wiki/sources/<slug>.md — one file per ingested source
TOKENS: {{SOURCE_DIR}}, {{PROCESSED_DIR}}, {{SOURCE_TYPES}}, {{DATE_TODAY}}, {{ENTRY_NOUN_PLURAL}}
Skeleton for hand-creating a source summary. A normal ingest writes these through the wiki-writer
agent instead; use this when recording a source outside an ingest, or as the format reference.
Copy the file, then delete this comment block — the `---` must be the first line of the finished
page, or the frontmatter will not parse.
-->
---
title: "[Full source title, as published]"
source_file: "{{SOURCE_DIR}}/exact-filename.md"
source_type: {{SOURCE_TYPES}}
date_ingested: {{DATE_TODAY}}
tags: [tag-one, tag-two]
entries_extracted: ["[[entry-one]]", "[[entry-two]]"]
---

## Summary

[2–3 sentences: what the source is, who made it, and what it contributed to the wiki. Note any
problem with the capture here too — truncated transcript, paywalled tail, images not retrieved.]

## Key Contributions

- **[Entry name]** — [one line on the idea this source uniquely supplied]
- **[Entry name]** — [one line]

## Entries Reinforced

- [[existing-entry]] — [what this source adds to a page that already existed]
- [[existing-entry]] — [a candidate idea that was dropped as a near-duplicate belongs here, not
  in a thin new page]

<!--
RULES FOR THIS PAGE TYPE

- This page is the record that the source was processed. It must exist before the raw file moves
  from `{{SOURCE_DIR}}/` to `{{PROCESSED_DIR}}/`, and it is what tells a later session not to
  ingest the same material twice.
- `source_file` is the exact filename of the raw source, character for character — odd
  punctuation, curly apostrophes, capitalisation and all. It is the only link back to the
  original. Do not tidy it, shorten it or guess it.
- `source_type` takes exactly one value from {{SOURCE_TYPES}}.
- Write this page even when the source yielded nothing: leave `entries_extracted` as `[]` and say
  why in the Summary (stub capture, link-index page, no extractable prose, verbatim duplicate).
  A missing page makes the source look permanently unprocessed.
- `entries_extracted` lists only pages actually created for this source, and every slug must exist.
  Reinforcements and genuine contradictions go under `## Entries Reinforced` instead — record a
  contradiction there rather than resolving it.
- The formatter agent never touches source summaries — Phase 3.5 is {{ENTRY_NOUN_PLURAL}} only —
  so what the writer produces here is final. Get the headings right first time.
- Field names are fixed: `title`, `source_file`, `source_type`, `date_ingested`, `tags`,
  `entries_extracted`. The reference implementation says `concepts_extracted:`; this kit does not.
- Slug: kebab-case, derived from the title rather than from a scraper-generated filename.

Full schema reference: docs/03-page-schemas.md. Worked example: examples/example-source-summary.md.
-->
